{:adr-id "2609300000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0144 (raising of sheep and goats) flock-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607154000" "ADR-2607152100" "ADR-2607122200" "ADR-2607011000"]

 :context
 "A prior agent, tasked with what it believed was ISIC 0144 (swine/pigs), discovered
  mid-build that the code was mislabeled: per the authoritative kotoba-lang/industry
  registry (matching the real UN ISIC Rev.4 standard), 0144 is 'Raising of sheep and
  goats' and 0145 is 'Raising of swine/pigs'. That agent's repo was renamed
  cloud-itonami-isic-0144 -> cloud-itonami-isic-0145 to fix the mislabel
  (ADR-2607154000), leaving the registry's 0144 entry (:maturity :spec, placeholder
  :repo/:business-id gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0144) genuinely untouched and
  unimplemented -- deferred for future coverage. This ADR is that future coverage.
  Live registry re-verified fresh before work began: :name 'Raising of sheep and
  goats' confirmed for {:id \"0144\"}. GitHub's rename-redirect made
  `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0144` return the renamed swine
  repo's data (full_name cloud-itonami-isic-0145) -- a false-positive 'exists' signal
  for the now-free name. `gh repo create cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0144`
  succeeded on the first attempt; the -livestock fallback name was not needed. Built
  from cloud-itonami-isic-0145 (swineops.*, the corrected sibling this task was
  explicitly pointed at) as the module-structure template."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct animal handling (farm operator's exclusive authority)"
  "veterinary treatment decisions (veterinarian/farm operator authority)"
  "culling decisions (economic and ethical authority remains human)"
  "disease-outbreak declarations / animal-health authority contact (actor only
    surfaces a flagged concern for human/veterinary judgment)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0144 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0145 module-for-module, adapted
  from swine-farming to sheep-and-goat farming -- flockops.* namespace, paddock/pen
  management, health/welfare vocabulary specialized to sheep/goat notifiable
  diseases instead of ASF/CSF/PRRS):
  - Governor (FlockOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (facility-not-registered,
    no-execution, treatment-or-culling-blocked, op-not-allowed,
    flock-count-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate health/welfare
    concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (feed/veterinary-supply/
    shearing-equipment), breeds with species tag (suffolk/merino = sheep,
    saanen/boer = goat), and a health/welfare-concern reference vocabulary
    (Scrapie/Bluetongue/FMD/Foot Rot) -- purely descriptive, never changes the
    Governor's disposition
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    flock-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-facility lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0145's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-husbandry-record (flock count/weight/health-check/offspring/
    fleece-weight data), schedule-farm-operation (grazing-rotation/shearing/
    breeding), flag-animal-health-concern (ALWAYS escalates, e.g. suspected
    Scrapie), order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 103 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store),
    all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-0144 (no rename needed)"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Sheep-and-goat raising (0144) now genuinely implemented and fully tested --
    closing the gap explicitly left open by ADR-2607154000"
   "Scope boundaries (animal handling, treatment, culling) hardcoded in governor
    checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Animal-health/welfare escalation (flag-animal-health-concern always human, e.g.
    suspected Scrapie) is a core design invariant; actor structurally cannot
    declare an outbreak or contact authorities itself"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0145's own stub status"]}

 :verification
 {:test-count 31
  :assertion-count 103
  :test-status "0 failures, 0 errors (clojure -M:test, scratch-dir build)"
  :lint-status "0 errors, 0 warnings (clojure -M:lint)"
  :repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0144"
  :repo-note "created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-0144 -- no rename fallback needed"
  :registry-update "kotoba-lang/industry: 0144 maturity :spec -> :implemented, repo/business-id corrected to cloud-itonami-isic-0144, ADR reference added -- SHAs recorded in the task's final report, not duplicated here"}}
